# React Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define component architecture and composition patterns
- Enforce Server vs Client Component boundaries
- Standardize React Query usage for client-side data
- Ensure reusable, accessible component design

## Best Practices

- **Server Components default** — add `"use client"` only for hooks, events, browser APIs
- **Composition over inheritance** — compound components for complex UI
- **Colocate state** — lift only when siblings need shared state
- **React Query** for client fetching, caching, optimistic updates
- **Custom hooks** extract reusable logic; components stay presentational
- **Error boundaries** wrap feature sections, not entire app

## Coding Standards

- One component per file (except tightly coupled sub-components)
- Props interface named `[Component]Props`
- Destructure props in function signature
- Early return for loading/error/empty states
- Memoize expensive computations with `useMemo`; callbacks with `useCallback` only when profiled necessary
- Keys on lists must be stable IDs, never array index

## Folder Structure

```
src/components/           # Shared, cross-feature UI
├── ui/                   # shadcn primitives (auto-generated)
├── layout/               # AppShell, Sidebar, Header
├── data-display/         # DataTable, StatCard, Timeline
├── feedback/             # EmptyState, ErrorFallback
└── forms/                # FormField wrappers

src/features/[feature]/ui/  # Feature-specific components
src/hooks/                  # Global hooks (useDebounce, useMediaQuery)
src/providers/              # QueryProvider, ThemeProvider
```

## Naming Convention

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Component file | PascalCase.tsx | `CaseList.tsx` |
| Client Component | Same + `"use client"` top | `CaseFilters.tsx` |
| Hook file | use*.ts | `useCases.ts` |
| Provider | *Provider.tsx | `QueryProvider.tsx` |
| Event handler | handle* | `handleSubmit` |
| Boolean prop | is/has/can prefix | `isLoading`, `hasError` |

## Performance Rules

- Split Client Components to smallest interactive island
- Virtualize lists >100 items (`@tanstack/react-virtual`)
- Debounce search inputs (300ms default)
- Avoid inline object/array literals in props to memoized children
- Prefetch on hover for navigation links via React Query

## Security Rules

- Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without DOMPurify
- Sanitize user content before display
- No secrets or tokens in Client Components

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — React Query hook
// features/cases/hooks/use-cases.ts
export function useCases(filters: CaseFilters) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['cases', filters],
    queryFn: () => getCases(filters),
    staleTime: 30_000,
  });
}

// ✅ GOOD — Presentational component with early returns
export function CaseList({ cases, isLoading }: CaseListProps) {
  if (isLoading) return <CaseListSkeleton />;
  if (!cases.length) return <EmptyState title="No cases" />;
  return (
    <ul role="list">
      {cases.map((c) => <CaseListItem key={c.id} case={c} />)}
    </ul>
  );
}

// ❌ BAD — Business logic in component
function CaseForm() {
  const total = items.reduce((s, i) => s + i.price * i.qty, 0); // move to util/service
}
```

## Things to Avoid

- `useEffect` for data fetching (use Server Components or React Query)
- Prop drilling >2 levels (use composition or context)
- Giant components mixing fetch, form, table, modal
- Default exports for hooks/utilities (named exports preferred)
- Suppressing React key warnings

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] `"use client"` only where necessary
- [ ] Loading, empty, and error states implemented
- [ ] Props fully typed with interface
- [ ] List items have stable keys
- [ ] Accessible markup (roles, labels, focus)
- [ ] No business logic that belongs in services/actions
